{
  "summary": "Check LevelDB iterator status in `txindex` during transaction lookups via `FindTx()`. It adds a `CDBIterator::CheckStatus()` helper that invokes `HandleError()` if an iterator encountered an underlying database error, throwing a `dbwrapper_error` instead of silently returning `nullopt`.",
  "problem": "When LevelDB encounters a database corruption or I/O error during a `txindex` iterator scan, the iterator becomes invalid. Because `FindTx()` only checked whether the iterator was valid rather than inspecting its status, underlying database read errors were indistinguishable from an absent transaction and returned `nullopt` instead of alerting the caller to a database failure.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description: 'LevelDB detected the corruption, but the same lookup returned `nullopt` instead of throwing. Restoring the original data made the lookup work again.'",
    "Follow-up to merged PR #35728 ('rpc: Properly throw on internal I/O errors in GetTransaction')."
  ],
  "dependencies": {
    "depends_on": [],
    "enables": []
  },
  "scope_notes": "Small 6-line change touching dbwrapper and txindex.",
  "changed_since_previous": "",
  "card": "txindex's FindTx method now checks LevelDB iterator error status before returning nullopt on lookup failure. Previously, if database corruption or an I/O error caused the iterator to fail, FindTx treated the transaction as simply not found rather than raising a database error. This follows up on PR 35728, which fixed similar error suppression in GetTransaction RPC handling.",
